# Global Mobile Responsiveness Audit & Overhaul

The Storyline website currently relies heavily on inline styles with large hardcoded values (e.g. `fontSize: '4.5rem'`, `width: '500px'`, large flex grid gaps) which look great on desktop but break layouts on mobile devices.

This plan details how I will systematically scan and overhaul the entire website to make it fully responsive on all devices without overwriting the design language or causing over-zoom issues.

## Proposed Changes

I will execute a multi-phase refactoring of the codebase:

### Phase 1: Global CSS Overhaul (`index.css` & `styles/components.css`)
- **Global Typography Scale**: I will introduce fluid typography (using `clamp()`) or strict media queries for `.mega-heading` and `.hero-body-text` so they automatically scale down on screens under 768px.
- **Horizontal Overflow Fixes**: I will strictly enforce `overflow-x: hidden` on the HTML/Body tags to prevent horizontal scrolling (the "overzoom" or "wobbly" effect on mobile).
- **Responsive Padding/Margins**: I will scale down the global CSS variables (`--space-3xl`, `--space-2xl`) on mobile devices so sections don't have massive empty gaps on small screens.

### Phase 2: Refactoring Inline Styles in JSX Files
Many React components use inline styles that force desktop layouts. I will scan and modify the following files:

- **`Home.jsx` & `About.jsx`**: 
  - Remove hardcoded `height: '600px'` and `width: '1200px'` constraints.
  - Convert side-by-side flex layouts to `flex-direction: column` for mobile.
- **`DesignStudio.jsx`**:
  - Replace hardcoded `fontSize: '4.5rem'` and `fontSize: '3rem'` with responsive CSS classes.
  - Ensure the grid layouts (the creative arsenal and the new asymmetric collage) correctly break down into 1 or 2 columns on mobile.
- **`Weddings.jsx` & `Corporate.jsx`**:
  - Fix any absolute positioning or static widths that cause text to overflow the screen.
  - Ensure the sequential service lists stack neatly.
- **`Hampers.jsx` & `Team.jsx`**:
  - Update grid columns to use `minmax(200px, 1fr)` or media queries so they wrap cleanly.

### Phase 3: Navbar & Navigation
- Ensure the mobile hamburger menu works flawlessly and the links are large enough to be easily tapped (touch targets).

## Verification Plan
- I will run a local build (`npm run build`) to ensure no React syntax errors were introduced.
- I will review the CSS to ensure media queries cover the standard breakpoints (max-width: 768px, max-width: 480px).

